{
  "name": "Track expenses from Telegram chat with AI and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track expenses from Telegram chat with AI and Google Sheets\n\nA personal expense tracker you talk to in plain language. Send \"coffee 25k\" or \"lunch 45000 and taxi 30000\" to your Telegram bot, and it records each item in Google Sheets with a date and category. Ask \"how much did I spend this week?\" or \"change the taxi to 35000\" and it reads or updates the sheet for you.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Telegram Trigger** receives each message.\n2. Only chat IDs in `allowedChatIds` can use the bot; anyone else gets their chat ID back so the owner can add it.\n3. An **AI Agent** (Google Gemini) with chat memory decides what to do and calls three Google Sheets tools: add, read and update.\n4. The reply goes back to Telegram. If the agent fails, the user gets a short apology instead of silence.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet with a tab named `Expenses` and the headers `ID`, `Date`, `Description`, `Category`, `Amount`.\n2. Fill in **Configuration**: spreadsheet ID, sheet name, currency and timezone.\n3. Add credentials: Telegram (bot token from @BotFather), Google Gemini (API key from Google AI Studio) and Google Sheets (OAuth2).\n4. Activate the workflow and message your bot. It replies with your chat ID: put it in `allowedChatIds`.\n\n### Customization\n- Edit categories, tone or rules in the agent's system message.\n- Swap Gemini for any other chat model node.\n\n**Limitations:** text messages only, no deleting rows, and summaries are calculated by the model, so double-check large totals.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "8186403a-2008-4f5b-95ec-90915290eafb",
